      "created_at": "2013-04-13T13:05:54.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>This came up in a recent game. I'm pretty sure we ruled correctly, but thought I'd check.</p><p>Triceratops deals damage \"to the target other than itself with the second highest HP\".</p><p>Does this mean: i) In the set of all targets excepting the triceratops, the target with the second lowest HP, OR ii) In the set of all targets, the target with the second lowest HP that is not the triceratops.</p><p>Example: Triceratops 8 HP, HeroA 10 HP, HeroB 12 HP.</p><p>Option i) HeroB takes damage. Option ii) HeroA takes damage</p><p>We ruled i), but the players brought up the question, so I figure I'd check for consensus.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
